      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: This name confused me at first because Porter-Duff blends are still represented as an SkBlendMode (at some level, not in the blender functions that uses coefficient uniforms). `needsBlendModeBased` is really any SkBlendMode that\u0027s not Porter-Duff. But we also have the advanced blend modes like hue, saturation, color, and luminosity.\n\nSkBlendMode defines three values `kLastCoeffMode` for porter duff, `kLastSeparableMode` for the remaining non-advanced mode, and then just `kLastMode` to have the advanced modes.\n\nI don\u0027t feel strongly about using Coefficient vs. Porter-Duff, although it does emphasize how the sksl effect is structured differently, but I think using `needsSeparableMode` would be clearer than `needsBlendMode`. Alternatively maybe we make this a bit field so we can OR in coefficient, separable, and (later?) advanced blend modes?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 83,
        "startChar": 31,
        "endLine": 83,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "3277bada62aaaa9de9e4ec2a451e50b07ec9f460",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
